Board P0/P1 consensus batch (4-director synthesis)

Strategy + Product + Engineering + AI Director synthesis from the
deferred-items review. Buffett, Trust, Jobs reviews stalled (watchdog
timeout, not content failure) — executing on the 4-director consensus
that landed.

ENGINEERING P0 (3 bugs blocking Friday):

1. acceptQuote status-flip ordering — status flipped first, then
   side effects. A failed schedule/alert left status='sold' with no
   calendar entry and no owner buzz. Customer thinks it worked,
   tenant never knows. Reordered: audit -> schedule -> alert ->
   status flip. Partial-failure path now lands the side effects
   first, so a status-flip retry on the already-sold path is a
   no-op (audit/schedule already idempotent). The bug that turns
   a $999 customer into a refund request is closed.

2. createInstallSlotForAcceptedQuote dual-path INSERT silently
   swallowed any error from the proposal_id INSERT, including RLS
   denial / FK violation. Now: only fall back when SQLSTATE 42703
   (undefined column) or matching message. Other errors structured-
   logged + return early; no double audit row.

3. pickNextMove computed twice per /app render — once for the
   priority_decision audit, once inside OwnersDailyOneLiner. A
   midnight-UTC clock straddle would have audit and CTA disagree.
   Fixed: page computes once and passes `move` prop to the
   component; component falls back to recomputing only if the prop
   is absent (preserves existing call-site contracts).

AI DIRECTOR P0:

4. priority_decision now rolled into the daily Merkle root
   (lib/audit/merkle.ts). AI Director's covenant: any future "did
   your AI pick this CTA on May 12?" question is now
   cryptographically answerable. Counts plumbed through RootSummary,
   transparency-snapshot cron writes priority_decisions_count when
   the column exists with PGRST204 fallback. Migration
   20260507_i_transparency_priority_count.sql adds the column.

5. /receipt/[id] SURFACE_LABELS gained "question-reply-draft":
   "Reply Suggestions". Receipt URLs in tenant emails now render a
   human label instead of the raw key.

6. AI reply suggestions (lib/ai/suggest-reply.ts):
   - JSON code-fence stripping before parse — Sonnet sometimes
     wraps JSON in ```json blocks despite the explicit instruction.
     Strip fences + extract outermost {...} as fallback.
   - Per-question idempotency cache: SHA-256 of (proposal+question),
     60s TTL, 500-entry LRU. A customer who hits Send twice within
     rate-limit no longer burns 5 Anthropic calls.
   - AI_REPLY_SUGGESTIONS_DISABLED env kill switch (defaults ON).
     Future tenants.tier check can layer on top.

PRODUCT P0:

7. AI suggestions moved ABOVE the question in the alert email.
   Product Director's unique read: variants are the action, the
   question is context. Tenant scans suggestions first, picks one,
   verifies against the customer's text right below. The card is
   no longer the buried last-scroll afterthought.

8. Email Gmail compatibility — every text node now has explicit
   color:#f5f5f5 so a stripped <style> block in Gmail web doesn't
   make the AI variants unreadable. Single receipt link kept (was
   two).

9. Phone normalization for SMS share — `customers.primary_phone`
   has parens/spaces in the wild; Android Chrome's intent handler
   chokes on those. Strip everything except digits and leading "+";
   require >=10 digits before showing the action.

10. Test-mode checkbox repositioned next to the Title label as a
    🧪 Test mode chip — visible above the fold on a 375px viewport
    instead of buried below 4 cards. Removed the duplicate label
    that was at the bottom of the form.

11. AcceptButton + AskQuestionForm rate_limited copy fixed — said
    "wait a minute" but the bucket refills in 12 seconds. Now
    "wait a few seconds and try again" (bilingual EN/ES).

STRATEGY P0 (regulatory):

12. AI disclosure under the question textarea — CCPA §1798.185(a)(16)
    + GDPR Article 22 require pre-processing notice for automated
    decision-making. Plain-language: "Your message goes to your
    contractor. We may use Claude (Anthropic) to draft suggested
    replies they can review before sending — they always have the
    final word." Bilingual EN/ES, links to /transparency.

ENGINEERING P1 (defensive):

13. log.ts JSON.stringify wrapped in safeJson() — circular-ref or
    unserializable values in the context object would have thrown
    inside the warn path. Now falls back to a tagged sentinel
    string so the warn line still lands.

14. parseBomRead now structured-logs to surface "bom.parse" /
    kind "fallback" when a non-null bom value fails validation.
    Existing-row shape problems no longer disappear silently.
    Logger import is dynamic to avoid pulling it into RSC graphs
    that don't otherwise need it.

USER ACTION REQUIRED before deploy:
  Apply 20260507_g, _h, _i migrations to live Supabase. Code is
  safe with or without all three (graceful fallbacks throughout).

